course: dictionary
lesson: 9
title: Body words: abdomen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The abdomen is the front part of your body, between your chest and your hips. It is the scientific word for your tummy or belly. «Pain in the abdomen» means a pain in your tummy.
explain: Insects have an abdomen too, but it is a different part. «An insect's body has a head, a thorax and an abdomen.» In an insect, the abdomen is the back section of the body, after the head and the thorax.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is used. If the sentence talks about legs, wings or feelers, it is about insects. If it talks about pain or muscles, it is about people. «Abdominal muscles» are tummy muscles, the ones people call abs.
fact: The abdomen is the part of the body between the chest and the hips.
fact: Your abdomen holds organs such as your stomach, intestines and liver.
fact: «Abdominal pain» means a tummy ache.
fact: «Abdominal muscles» are tummy muscles, often called abs.
fact: An adult insect has three body parts: head, thorax and abdomen.
fact: Spiders have two body parts, and they make silk in glands in the abdomen.
exercise: «An insect's body has a head, a thorax and an abdomen.» Which part is at the back of the insect? | wings | thorax | *abdomen | head
exercise: What does «abdominal pain» mean? | a sore throat | a sore head | *a tummy ache | a broken leg
exercise: Where do spiders make their silk? | in the head | in the legs | *in the abdomen | on the wrists
test: «Abdominal muscles» are which muscles? | neck muscles | *tummy muscles | arm muscles | leg muscles
test: How many body parts does an adult insect have? | six | four | *three | two
exam: «Every adult insect has six legs and a body in three parts.» Which word names the back part of an insect's body? | feelers | thorax | head | *abdomen
